</span></div>
</figure>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Methodology</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we establish the hardness of the representative agent selection problem and prove the submodularity of our objective function. We then discuss how naive applications of existing strategies are insufficient and present improved methods in Section <a href="#S4.SS2" title="4.2 Our Proposed Methods ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.2</span></a>. The performance guarantees and time complexity of the methods discussed in this section are summarized in Table <a href="#S3.T1" title="Table 1 ‣ 3.2 Objective ‣ 3 Problem Formulation ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Hardness of the Problem and Connection to Submodularity</h3>

<div id="Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(NP-Hardness)<span id="Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The problem of selecting an optimal subset <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\subseteq\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\subseteq\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes <math id="Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)</annotation></semantics></math> is NP-hard.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof sketch</span>. We show NP-hardness through a reduction from the uncapacitated facility location problem (UFLP) with zero facility costs, which is known to be NP-hard <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib36" title="" class="ltx_ref">Verter, 2011</a>)</cite>. We provide a detailed proof of this proposition in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS1" title="D.1 Proof of Theorem 1 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Submodularity of the Objective Function <math id="Thmproposition1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The objective function <math id="Thmproposition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]</annotation></semantics></math> is submodular.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof sketch</span>. Our objective function <math id="S4.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)</annotation></semantics></math> exhibits the diminishing returns property of submodularity, which follows directly from its connection to the facility location problem <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Krause &amp; Golovin, 2014</a>)</cite>. We provide proof of this proposition in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS2" title="D.2 Proof of Proposition 1 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Greedy Approximation</span>.
Due to the NP-hardness of the problem, finding the optimal solution <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\text{opt}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>L</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\text{opt}}</annotation></semantics></math> requires exhaustive search with time complexity <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}((|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|)^{KM})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}((|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|)^{KM})</annotation></semantics></math>.
The submodularity of our objective function enables the <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Greedy</span> algorithm to achieve a <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(1-1/e)\cdot f(L^{\text{opt}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>L</mi><mtext>opt</mtext></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(1-1/e)\cdot f(L^{\text{opt}})</annotation></semantics></math>-approximation guarantee <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nemhauser et al., 1978</a>)</cite>, with time complexity <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(M\cdot|\mathcal{H}|\cdot(|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|)^{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(M\cdot|\mathcal{H}|\cdot(|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|)^{K})</annotation></semantics></math>.
However, this approach becomes intractable as the agent space grows.
A stochastic variant, <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">StochasticGreedy</span>, samples a subset of agents at each iteration to approximate the solution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mirzasoleiman et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, but this still remains impractical for large spaces.
Inspired by <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Singla et al., 2014</a>; <a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mirzasoleiman et al., 2015</a>)</cite>, we adopt <span id="S4.SS1.p3.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">SampleGreedy</span>, which fixes a candidate pool <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> containing only a fraction <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ψ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi</annotation></semantics></math> of agents from <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and applies greedy selection within this pool.
At each round, the marginal contribution of each remaining agent in <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> is evaluated relative to the current set, and the best agent is added.
This process continues until <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> agents are selected.
The time complexity is <math id="S4.SS1.p3.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(M\cdot|\mathcal{H}|\cdot\psi\cdot(|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|)^{K})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ψ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>K</mi></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(M\cdot|\mathcal{H}|\cdot\psi\cdot(|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|)^{K})</annotation></semantics></math>, which is still impractical for large populations and motivates the more efficient methods introduced in the next section.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> Greedy selection of demonstrations (<math id="alg1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{demo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{demo}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algx1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Human set <math id="algx1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, human demonstrations <math id="algx1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of agents to select <math id="algx1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, context size <math id="algx1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> A set of representative agents <math id="algx1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\subseteq\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\subseteq\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algx1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="algx1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algx1.l4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Initialize <math id="algx1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx1.l5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Best set of K demonstrations found so far</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <span id="algx1.l6.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algx1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
               <math id="algx1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="demo^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{demo\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}\setminus\Omega}f(L\cup\{l_{\Omega\cup\{demo\}}\})-f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">demo^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{demo\in\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}\setminus\Omega}f(L\cup\{l_{\Omega\cup\{demo\}}\})-f(L)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l7.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx1.l7.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Select demo.</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
               <math id="algx1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega\leftarrow\Omega\cup\{demo^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>o</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega\leftarrow\Omega\cup\{demo^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <math id="algx1.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\leftarrow L\cup\{l_{\Omega}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\leftarrow L\cup\{l_{\Omega}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx1.l9.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx1.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx1.l9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Add agent with context <math id="algx1.l9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math> to solution set</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx1.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="algx1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Greedy selection of human-mapped agents (<math id="alg2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="alg2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}</annotation></semantics></math>)</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.4" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="algx2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">1:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx2.l1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Input:</span> Human set <math id="algx2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, human demonstrations <math id="algx2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>, number of agents to select <math id="algx2.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>, context size <math id="algx2.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">2:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx2.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Output:</span> A set of representative agents <math id="algx2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\subseteq\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\subseteq\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="algx2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|L|\leq M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|L|\leq M</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">3:</span>
              
              
             Initialize <math id="algx2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="algx2.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="algx2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">4:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx2.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each human <math id="algx2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">5:</span>
              
              
              Create agent <math id="algx2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> using a subset of K demonstrations from <math id="algx2.l5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{h}^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{h}^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>
<span id="algx2.l5.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx2.l5.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Human-mapped agent</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">6:</span>
              
              
              <math id="algx2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\cup\{l_{h}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\leftarrow\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\cup\{l_{h}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l6.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx2.l6.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Add the agent to pool</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">7:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="algx2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="algx2.l7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>



</div>
<div id="algx2.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">8:</span>
              
              
              <math id="algx2.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{l\in\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\setminus L}f(L\cup\{l\})-f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∖</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>l</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{*}\leftarrow\arg\max_{l\in\tilde{\mathcal{L}}\setminus L}f(L\cup\{l\})-f(L)</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l8.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx2.l8.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Select agent</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">9:</span>
              
              
              <math id="algx2.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L\leftarrow L\cup\{l^{*}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L\leftarrow L\cup\{l^{*}\}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="algx2.l9.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="algx2.l9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math><span id="algx2.l9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;"> Add agent to solution set</span>
</span>
</div>
<div id="algx2.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline">10:</span>
              
              
             <span id="algx2.l10.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span>  <math id="algx2.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Our Proposed Methods</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Greedy selection of demonstrations for an agent’s context</span>.
Searching through the exponentially large agent space <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> is computationally infeasible, limiting the practicality of standard greedy methods.
Hence, we propose an alternative method, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{demo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{demo}}</annotation></semantics></math> (<span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Rep</span>resentative <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Pop</span>ulation using <span id="S4.SS2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">demo</span>nstration-level greedy selection), which reduces the complexity to <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(M\cdot K\cdot|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(M\cdot K\cdot|\mathcal{T}|\cdot|\mathcal{H}|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> and empirically achieves competitive performance. Instead of enumerating all candidate agents and evaluating their marginal gains, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{demo}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>demo</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{demo}}</annotation></semantics></math> builds each agent incrementally (cf. Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ 4.1 Hardness of the Problem and Connection to Submodularity ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>). At each step it greedily selects a demonstration from the pool <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{\mathcal{H}}^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math> to extend the current context <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>. We denote by <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{\Omega}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{\Omega}</annotation></semantics></math> the agent constructed from <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Omega" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Omega</annotation></semantics></math>.
This demonstration-level greedy construction avoids the exponential blow-up in <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\mathcal{L}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\mathcal{L}|</annotation></semantics></math>, but sacrifices the formal performance guarantee of standard greedy selection.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Greedy selection of human-mapped agents.</span> To further address the computational intractability of searching the full agent space <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, we introduce a reduced pool of proxies that directly reflect the humans in the population. We construct <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}=\{l_{h}\mid h\in\mathcal{H}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}=\{l_{h}\mid h\in\mathcal{H}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, where each agent <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> corresponds to a human <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and is formed by conditioning on a subset of <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations from <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}_{h}^{\mathcal{T}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>h</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}_{h}^{\mathcal{T}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This one-to-one mapping reduces the candidate space to <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\tilde{\mathcal{L}}|=|\mathcal{H}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\tilde{\mathcal{L}}|=|\mathcal{H}|</annotation></semantics></math> while preserving diversity. The selection problem then becomes <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}=\arg\max_{L\subseteq\tilde{\mathcal{L}},|L|\leq M}f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}=\arg\max_{L\subseteq\tilde{\mathcal{L}},|L|\leq M}f(L)</annotation></semantics></math>. Building on this human-centered mapping idea, we instantiate two methods, <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, which both follow the general procedure in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ 4.1 Hardness of the Problem and Connection to Submodularity ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>. Their only difference lies in how demonstrations are selected to construct a human-mapped agent (line 5). In <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations for each human are sampled uniformly at random, yielding lightweight proxy agents with cost <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(K|\mathcal{H}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(K|\mathcal{H}|)</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}</annotation></semantics></math> selects the <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>K</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K</annotation></semantics></math> demonstrations greedily with respect to the human’s own behavior, producing stronger proxies at cost <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(K|\mathcal{T}||\mathcal{H}|)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(K|\mathcal{T}||\mathcal{H}|)</annotation></semantics></math>. Concretely, for each human <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, the demonstrations are chosen to minimize the distance between the human’s embedding <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> and the embedding of the constructed agent <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{e}_{l_{h}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{e}_{l_{h}}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l_{h}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l_{h}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Both methods share the same greedy selection stage over the proxy pool, which requires <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(M|\mathcal{H}|^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(M|\mathcal{H}|^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> time, and both enjoy the same approximation guarantee in Theorem <a href="#Thmtheorem2" title='Theorem 2 (Performance Guarantee for "RepPop"_"mapped-1" and "RepPop"_"mapped-2"). ‣ 4.2 Our Proposed Methods ‣ 4 Methodology ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations' class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span></span><span id="Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Performance Guarantee for <math id="Thmtheorem2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="Thmtheorem2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}</annotation></semantics></math>)<span id="Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}=\{l_{h}|h\in\mathcal{H}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}=\{l_{h}|h\in\mathcal{H}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the proxy agent set where for each <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{h}\in N_{\rho}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{h}\in N_{\rho}(h)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\rho}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\rho}(h)</annotation></semantics></math> representing the <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the human coverage ratio <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})/f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})/f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal subset from the human set and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal subset from the full agent set. If <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">greedy</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of size <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> returned by the greedy algorithm on <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</span></p>
<table id="S4.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\;\;\geq\;\;(1-1/e)\,\big(\,\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})-\rho\,\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">greedy</mtext></msubsup><mo rspace="0.560em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.838em">≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" rspace="0.170em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\;\;\geq\;\;(1-1/e)\,\big(\,\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})-\rho\,\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmtheorem2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> measures the cost of restricting the search space to humans (coverage quality) and <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> measures the cost of approximating each human by a proxy agent (imitation error). The value of <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math> is determined by how expressive the human set is relative to the full agent space, whereas <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> depends on the proxy construction strategy: uniform sampling in <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">mapped-1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> typically yields larger <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>, while greedy selection in <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">mapped-2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}</annotation></semantics></math> achieves smaller <math id="Thmtheorem2.p1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> at the expense of higher computational cost.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Proof sketch</span>. We show that for the optimal human subset <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the corresponding set of proxy agents <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}}=\{l_{h}|h\in L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}\}\subseteq\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊆</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}}=\{l_{h}|h\in L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}\}\subseteq\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-\rho</annotation></semantics></math> due to the <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood property. Since <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is optimal within <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})</annotation></semantics></math>. By the standard greedy approximation for submodular functions, <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-1/e)f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>greedy</mtext></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-1/e)f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Combining these inequalities and using the human coverage ratio <math id="S4.SS2.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})/f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>/</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})/f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})</annotation></semantics></math>, we derive our bound. We provide complete proof in Appendix <a href="#A4.SS3" title="D.3 Proof of Theorem 2 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D.3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Experimental Evaluation</h2>

<figure id="S5.T2" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 2: </span>Statistics of datasets used in our experiments.</figcaption>
<div id="S5.T2.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:24.2pt;vertical-align:-10.9pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-205.5pt,12.5pt) scale(0.491664091286351,0.491664091286351) ;">
