<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proofs</h2>

<section id="A4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Proof of Theorem 1</h3>

<div id="A4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 1</span> (NP-Hardness).
The problem of selecting an optimal subset <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}\subseteq\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}\subseteq\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> of size <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes <math id="A4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)</annotation></semantics></math> is NP-hard.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We show NP-hardness through a reduction from the k-facility location problem which extends the uncapacitated facility location problem (UFLP) by including a constraint on the maximum number of facilities. The problem is known to be NP-hard. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fowler et al., 1981</a>)</cite></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Consider an instance of the k-facility location problem with a set of potential facility locations <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}=\{f_{1},f_{2},\ldots,f_{n_{F}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>F</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}=\{f_{1},f_{2},\ldots,f_{n_{F}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, a set of customers <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{C}=\{c_{1},c_{2},\ldots,c_{n_{C}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><msub><mi>n</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{C}=\{c_{1},c_{2},\ldots,c_{n_{C}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>, service costs <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d(f,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d(f,c)</annotation></semantics></math> representing the cost of serving customer <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>c</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c</annotation></semantics></math> from facility <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, and a cardinality constraint <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math>. The objective is to select a subset <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F\subseteq\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F\subseteq\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> facilities to minimize the sum of service costs <math id="A4.SS1.p3.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\min_{f\in F}d(f,c)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{c\in\mathcal{C}}\min_{f\in F}d(f,c)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We construct a corresponding instance of our representative agent selection problem as follows: set <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}=\mathcal{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}=\mathcal{C}</annotation></semantics></math> (each customer corresponds to a human); set <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}=\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math> (each potential facility location corresponds to a potential agent); define <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})=d(l,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})=d(l,h)</annotation></semantics></math> for each human <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and agent <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>; and set <math id="A4.SS1.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> to be the number of facilities we wish to open.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Under this construction, our objective function becomes:</span></p>
<table id="A4.EGx1" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex2"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(L)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex3"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\left(\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}D_{\max}\right)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\left(\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}D_{\max}\right)-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex4"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=D_{\max}-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=D_{\max}-\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS1.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{\max}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{\max}</annotation></semantics></math> is a constant and <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}</annotation></semantics></math> is a positive constant, maximizing <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)</annotation></semantics></math> is equivalent to minimizing <math id="A4.SS1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\min_{l\in L}d(l,h)</annotation></semantics></math>, which is the objective of the k-facility location problem.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS1.p7" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, if the representative agent selection problem could be solved in polynomial time, the k-facility location problem could also be solved in polynomial time. Since the k-facility location problem is NP-hard, the representative agent selection problem must also be NP-hard.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.2 </span>Proof of Proposition 1</h3>

<div id="A4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span> (Submodularity).
The objective function</p>
<table id="A4.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">is submodular.</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">A set function <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is submodular if for all <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq B\subseteq\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq B\subseteq\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and for all <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}\in\mathcal{L}\setminus B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}\in\mathcal{L}\setminus B</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)\geq f(B\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)\geq f(B\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(B)</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Let <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq B\subseteq\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq B\subseteq\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}\in\mathcal{L}\setminus B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∖</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}\in\mathcal{L}\setminus B</annotation></semantics></math>. The marginal gain of adding <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in A\cup\{l^{\prime}\}}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\left(D_{\max}-\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right)\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in A\cup\{l^{\prime}\}}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\left(D_{\max}-\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">This simplifies to:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\min_{l\in A\cup\{l^{\prime}\}}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\min_{l\in A\cup\{l^{\prime}\}}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">Define <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}=\{h\in\mathcal{H}\mid\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})&lt;\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}=\{h\in\mathcal{H}\mid\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})&lt;\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\}</annotation></semantics></math> as the set of humans for whom <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> provides improvement when added to <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>. Similarly define <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math> for set <math id="A4.SS2.p5.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">For humans in <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the closest agent in <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> remains closer than <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="A4.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{l\in A\cup\{l^{\prime}\}}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})=\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{l\in A\cup\{l^{\prime}\}}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})=\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>, giving zero marginal improvement. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\subseteq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>⊆</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\subseteq B</annotation></semantics></math>, for any human <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\geq\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\geq\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">This implies that if <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> provides improvement over <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>), then <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> also provides improvement over <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> (i.e., <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>). Therefore, <math id="A4.SS2.p8.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}\subseteq\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">For humans in <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}</annotation></semantics></math>, the improvement when adding <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> is at least as large as when adding <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>, since <math id="A4.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\geq\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\geq\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Similarly, for <math id="A4.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(B\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(B)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></munder><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(B\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(B)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex10X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f(A\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(A)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex10Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex10Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>A</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup><mo>∖</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>[</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></msub><mi>dist</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>dist</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{A}^{l^{\prime}}\setminus\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in A}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex10Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mi>B</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msubsup></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\geq\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}_{B}^{l^{\prime}}}\left[\min_{l\in B}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})-\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l^{\prime}})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A4.Ex10Xd"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex10Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=f(B\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(B)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>l</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=f(B\cup\{l^{\prime}\})-f(B)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">This shows that <math id="A4.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is submodular.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.3 </span>Proof of Theorem 2</h3>

<div id="A4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 2</span> (Performance Guarantee for <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}</annotation></semantics></math>).
Let <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}=\{l_{h}|h\in\mathcal{H}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}=\{l_{h}|h\in\mathcal{H}\}</annotation></semantics></math> be the proxy agent set where for each <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{h}\in N_{\rho}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{h}\in N_{\rho}(h)</annotation></semantics></math>, with <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{\rho}(h)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{\rho}(h)</annotation></semantics></math> representing the <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. Define the human coverage ratio <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})}{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})}{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal subset from the human set and <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal subset from the full agent set. If <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mtext>greedy</mtext></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{\text{greedy}}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of size <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> returned by the greedy algorithm on <math id="A4.SS3.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>, then:</p>
<table id="A4.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})(\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})-\rho)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})(\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">In our context, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}\subseteq\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>⊆</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}\subseteq\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the optimal subset of humans of size <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> that would be selected if we directly choose humans instead of agents. This is a theoretical construct for analysis purposes. In contrast, <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal subset of size <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> from the actual agent set <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>. The human coverage ratio <math id="A4.SS3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})}{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})}\in[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})}{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})}\in[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> measures how well selecting from the human set can approximate the optimal solution achievable using the full agent set.
We start our proof by first decomposing the objective function as</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L)=\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}f_{h}(L)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L)=\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}f_{h}(L)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.SS3.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{h}(L)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{h}(L)=\frac{1}{|\mathcal{H}|}\left[D_{\max}-\min_{l\in L}\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l})\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">For each human <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math> in the optimal subset <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}</annotation></semantics></math>, consider its corresponding agent <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> in the proxy agent set <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A4.SS3.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}}=\{l_{h}|h\in L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}}=\{l_{h}|h\in L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}}\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">By definition, for each human <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h\in\mathcal{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h\in\mathcal{H}</annotation></semantics></math> and its corresponding proxy agent <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{h}\in\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{h}\in\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l_{h}})\leq\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>dist</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\operatorname{dist}(\mathbf{e}_{h},\mathbf{e}_{l_{h}})\leq\rho</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l_{h}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>l</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l_{h}</annotation></semantics></math> is in the <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood of <math id="A4.SS3.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>h</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f_{h}(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f_{h}(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})|\leq\frac{\rho}{|\mathcal{H}|}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f_{h}(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f_{h}(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})|\leq\frac{\rho}{|\mathcal{H}|}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">The above inequality holds because the maximum distance deviation between any human and its proxy agent is at most <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math> (by definition of the <math id="A4.SS3.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>-neighborhood).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Then:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})|=\left|\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}f_{h}(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f_{h}(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\right|\leq\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}|f_{h}(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f_{h}(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})|\leq\frac{\rho}{|\mathcal{H}|}\cdot|\mathcal{H}|=\rho" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mi>ρ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})|=\left|\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}f_{h}(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f_{h}(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\right|\leq\sum_{h\in\mathcal{H}}|f_{h}(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-f_{h}(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})|\leq\frac{\rho}{|\mathcal{H}|}\cdot|\mathcal{H}|=\rho</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">This gives us:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-\rho" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-\rho</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the optimal subset of size <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> from the proxy agent set <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>,
and <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is a feasible solution of size <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> from <math id="A4.SS3.p8.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the guarantees of the greedy algorithm for submodular function maximization <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib24" title="" class="ltx_ref">Nemhauser et al., 1978</a>)</cite>, if <math id="A4.SS3.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}}</annotation></semantics></math> is the subset of size <math id="A4.SS3.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> returned by the greedy algorithm on <math id="A4.SS3.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</span></p>
<table id="A4.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text">Combining inequalities equation <a href="#A4.E2" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem 2 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, equation <a href="#A4.E3" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem 2 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>, and equation <a href="#A4.E4" title="In Proof. ‣ D.3 Proof of Theorem 2 ‣ Appendix D Proofs ‣ Prompt Optimization Across Multiple Agents for Representing Diverse Human Populations" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>, we get:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\\
\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\\
\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})(f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-\rho)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\\
\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})f(L^{*}_{\tilde{\mathcal{H}}})\\
\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})(f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.SS3.p11.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text">Using the definition of human coverage ratio <math id="A4.SS3.p11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma=\frac{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})}{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma=\frac{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})}{f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A4.SS3.p11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})=\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{H}})=\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})</annotation></semantics></math>. Substitution yields</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})(\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})-\rho)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>e</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>L</mi><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ρ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(L^{greedy}_{\tilde{\mathcal{L}}})\geq(1-\frac{1}{e})(\gamma\cdot f(L^{*}_{\mathcal{L}})-\rho)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.SS3.p12" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.SS3.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.SS3.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text">This gives us the performance guarantees for <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-1</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-1}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.SS3.p12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mtext class="ltx_font_smallcaps">RepPop</mtext><mtext>mapped-2</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\textsc{RepPop}_{\text{mapped-2}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
